<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petro Shelest</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1996">1996</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petro Shelest was first secretary of the Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> from 1963 to 1972. While loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, he defended Ukrainian economic interests and tolerated some promotion of Ukrainian language and culture. He was removed in 1972, accused of nationalist leanings, and replaced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volodymyr-shcherbytsky">Volodymyr Shcherbytsky</a>, who led a renewed campaign of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russification">Russification</a>.</p></div>
